  "notes": "The consonant end of West Coast loop production and, per the research, the least minor-heavy producer in the whole section — so this is the only entry on this axis whose `scales` lead with `major` and whose keys are spelled major. Three parameters carry the \"smoothed-out\" description: the hats are the quietest here (`velocities.main` topping out at 0.75 where the parent reaches 0.95), the note density is low because the method is long, largely unaltered 4-bar sample loops with minimal overdubs, and the bass does not counter-line — his documented habit is to enhance the sample with added bass following its root motion, which is `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.9. ⛔ It is 0.9 and not 1.0 on purpose: the bass part still owes a reachable pool, so the register spans 18 semitones and the roots come from more than one chord. ⚠ The Imaj7–IVmaj7 reading is the research's own; the ii–V family is INFERRED from the 70s soul source vocabulary and carries the lowest weight. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates him high-medium: the sample sources and the added-bass method are documented, the tempo band and the drum velocities are catalog-level readings.",
